# Zealakit Overlay conventions

- `@zealakit/overlay-core` is framework-independent. Never import React / Vue / Svelte from it.
- Adapters (`vanilla`, `react`, `vue`, `svelte`) depend on core with `workspace:^`; core depends
  on no adapter. Keep the dependency graph acyclic.
- SSR safety: no `window` / `document` access at module init or during render. Use
  `isBrowser()` for guards and framework lifecycle hooks for DOM effects.
- Do not ship default CSS or a styling system. Styling is the consumer's job (`data-*` hooks OK).
- Only `@zealakit/overlay-core` may import the positioning engine (`@floating-ui/dom`). Adapters
  consume `createPositioner()`; keep engine types out of public adapter APIs.
- New core primitives ship with focused tests (`pnpm test`). Do not add a second test framework.
- Do not export unimplemented APIs, placeholder components, or a positioning engine that is not
  actually implemented.
- TypeScript only: `type` aliases, `import type`, strict mode, ESM. Files are `kebab-case`.
- Build order matters: core emits `dist` first; adapters resolve core through its package
  exports. Run `pnpm build` before `pnpm typecheck`.
- Verify with `pnpm check` (build + typecheck + test + lint) before reporting work as done.
  Run the relevant example/docs builds when those areas change.
- `examples/` are integration/smoke-test projects only. Product documentation lives only in the
  root and package READMEs (EN, VI, CN); there is no `docs/` folder and no separate docs app.
- Load the compact `.agents/skills/overlay/SKILL.md` before code, test, docs, or release work,
  and `.agents/skills/readme-system/SKILL.md` before touching any README. Run
  `pnpm readme:check` after README changes.
- Update the READMEs, `.agents/AGENTS.md`, and `.agents/skills/overlay/SKILL.md` together when
  architecture, package boundaries, commands, or documented workflows change.
